  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 145 PM MDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nFor Sunday through Wednesday, modest westerly flow persists aloft, \nas a few more disturbances translate across the Northern Tier. \nModel data does indicate enough residual moisture to support chances\nof showers over and near the higher terrain, with the best coverage \nalong and west of the ContDvd. Otherwise, after a slight cool down \non Sunday, especially across the plains with low level upslope in \nplace, temperatures to remain at and above seasonal levels through \nthe middle of the week.   \n\nBy the end of the week and into next weekend, longer range model \ndata supports increasing southwest flow across the Rockies, as an\nEastern Pacific system moving onshore across the Pacific Northwest\nCoast, digs into the Great Basin. Where is goes from there remains \nuncertain, however, the increasing southwest flow will help keep \ntemperatures at and above seasonal levels, with increasing chances \nof precipitation along and west of the ContDvd likely. Time will\ntell.",
